  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\frac{d y}{d x}=y+3>0$ and $y(0)=2$, then $y(\\ln 2)$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n5\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n13\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n-2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n7",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{d y}{d x}=y+3 \\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{y+3}=d x$\n$\\ln (y+3)=x+c$\n$x=0 \\Rightarrow y=2$\n$\\Rightarrow \\ln 5=0+c$\n$c=\\ln 5$\n$\\ln (y+3)=x+\\ln 5$\n$y+3=e^{x+\\ln 5} \\Rightarrow y+3=e^{\\ln 2+\\ln 5}$\n$y+3=10 \\Rightarrow y=7$"
  }
